systemd-sysupdate, systemd-sysupdated and updatectl as standalone binaries, linked statically
against systemd's own libraries the way systemd-repart.standalone is.

Wolfi's systemd is built with -Dsysupdate=disabled, so spindrift builds them on its own.
Upstream v261.3 has no standalone targets for them; the normal ones link
libsystemd-shared-261.so, which would tie the package to the exact build of Wolfi's systemd.
The standalone ones carry what they need and only take the system libraries they name.
systemd-sysupdated is the D-Bus service (org.freedesktop.sysupdate1) GNOME Software's
systemd-sysupdate plugin updates the OS through; updatectl is its command line.

